1
00:00:01,089 --> 00:00:02,765
亲爱的 要我把车开出去吗
Honey, do you need me to move the car?

2
00:00:02,765 --> 00:00:04,165
不 不用 我能行
No, it's nothing. I'm alright

3
00:00:04,635 --> 00:00:08,947
不 铁十字给我力量 它要栽了
Oh no! Iron cross, she's going down

4
00:00:09,284 --> 00:00:10,868
当心 菲尔
Oh god! Phil...

5
00:00:15,947 --> 00:00:17,868
-你没事吧 -没事
- You okay? - Yes. I am.

6
00:00:17,909 --> 00:00:19,237
我没事
I am okay.

7
00:00:19,268 --> 00:00:20,668
亲爱的 我们为什么要留着这辆车
Honey, why do we keep this car?

8
00:00:20,698 --> 00:00:21,771
这车老经典了
It's a classic!

9
00:00:21,771 --> 00:00:22,844
不 它只是空占地方
No, it just sits here.

10
00:00:22,854 --> 00:00:24,622
安全带也坏了
And the seatbelts don't work.

11
00:00:24,673 --> 00:00:26,605
门也卡 还漏油
The doors stick. It leaks fluids.

12
00:00:26,635 --> 00:00:28,321
我们也十年没给它加过油了
We haven't put fluids in it in 10 years.

13
00:00:28,373 --> 00:00:30,488
我会把这些毛病都修好
Well, I'm gonna fix all that anyway.

14
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:33,022
然后 送给海莉
And then, uh, it's gonna be Haley's car.

15
00:00:33,063 --> 00:00:34,974
我才不要给海莉
Oh, we're not giving this car to Haley.

16
00:00:35,004 --> 00:00:37,201
车后座都宽得可以放床垫了
It's way too easy to fit a mattress in the back.

17
00:00:37,242 --> 00:00:39,133
当年这车可是我们的洞房啊
Remember?

18
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:40,696
要命了 这车必须卖
Oh, no. We're selling it.

19
00:00:40,696 --> 00:00:41,565
什么
What?!

20
00:00:41,565 --> 00:00:43,159
除非你觉得你卖不出
Unless you don't think you can.

21
00:00:43,363 --> 00:00:44,876
-此话当真 -是的
- Really? - Yeah.

22
00:00:44,876 --> 00:00:46,204
-确定当真 -绝对当真
- Seriously? - You can't.

23
00:00:46,224 --> 00:00:48,033
你确定我卖不掉
You honestly think that's gonna work?

24
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:49,310
就是卖不掉
You can't sell it.

25
00:00:53,643 --> 00:00:54,931
话说
You know what?

26
00:00:54,931 --> 00:00:56,760
你怎么羞辱我都可以
You can insult a lot of things about me...

27
00:00:56,811 --> 00:00:59,498
发型啊 声音啊 平衡板游戏啥的
My hair, my voice, my balance-board exercises...

28
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:00,888
就是不要羞辱我强大的销售能力
But don't insult my selling.

29
00:01:00,919 --> 00:01:02,717
过分了哈
That crosses a line.

30
00:01:02,717 --> 00:01:04,454
过在哪里 你瞧不见?
What line? Oh, you don't see it?

31
00:01:04,454 --> 00:01:05,773
因为我以光速给它卖了
That's 'cause I just sold it.

32
00:01:20,457 --> 00:01:22,817
当这个美黑小星星声称
While the spray-tanned starlet claims

33
00:01:22,817 --> 00:01:26,271
自己有六个星期没嗑药时 知情者爆料道
to be six weeks sober, sources down under say:

34
00:01:26,302 --> 00:01:29,020
她就像一个嗑药过量的袋鼠一样
She has been bar-hopping

35
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:29,981
蹦啊跳啊混迹于酒吧
like a coked-up kangaroo."

36
00:01:30,021 --> 00:01:32,954
爹地给你读什么呢
Ah, what's daddy reading to you?

37
00:01:32,964 --> 00:01:34,334
如果还要我再读一次
If I have to read "the very hungry caterpillar"

38
00:01:34,334 --> 00:01:35,642
《饥肠辘辘的毛毛虫》 我会抓狂的
One more time, I will snap.

39
00:01:35,642 --> 00:01:38,033
-哪有那么差劲啊 -别逼人家
- oh, it's not that bad. - I will snap!

40
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:41,354
那啥 我把工具箱拿到外面了
So, um, I laid the toolbox outside,

41
00:01:41,354 --> 00:01:42,437
所有的材料也都准备好了
And all the supplies are ready,

42
00:01:42,437 --> 00:01:44,440
可以开工了
And I think we are good to go!

43
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,278
好极了
Terrific.

44
00:01:45,278 --> 00:01:47,403
你不打算换身工人套装吗
Aren't you gonna change into a working man's outfit?

45
00:01:47,403 --> 00:01:48,241
不用了
No, I'm good,

46
00:01:48,241 --> 00:01:50,581
况且我不觉得工人管它叫"套装"
And I don't think workmen really call them "outfits."

47
00:01:50,612 --> 00:01:54,270
我们要给莉莉建一座公主城堡
We are building a princess castle for Lily.

48
00:01:54,771 --> 00:01:58,082
这是每个父亲都想给他女儿建的
Uh, it's something every father wants to be able to do for his daughter.

49
00:01:58,112 --> 00:02:00,984
并且 我把自己幻想成
You know, and I fancy myself

50
00:02:00,984 --> 00:02:03,722
这个城堡的设计师
as a bit of a castle designer.

51
00:02:03,722 --> 00:02:05,715
我画了一些草图
I have done a few sketches.

52
00:02:05,756 --> 00:02:10,487
那些以备后用 这样我们就能用组装套件
Which we have archived so we can use the kit.

53
00:02:10,528 --> 00:02:12,235
-对 -套件
- Mm, yeah. - The kit.

54
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:14,513
套件 我们夫妇一条心一起做
Uh, the kit. Which, uh, we're gonna do together.

55
00:02:14,544 --> 00:02:16,823
要跟米奇尔一起做这个还不如杀了我
I am petrified to do this with Mitchell.

56
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:20,788
他大学的时候做过几个戏剧的布景什么的
He built a couple of theater sets in college or something,

57
00:02:20,788 --> 00:02:22,617
就以为自己是建筑帝了
And now he thinks he knows everything about building.

58
00:02:25,846 --> 00:02:28,114
但他根本不搭边
Well, he doesn't.

59
00:02:28,155 --> 00:02:31,047
每次我们家要做改造
Every home-improvement project that we've undertaken.

60
00:02:31,088 --> 00:02:33,060
都让人好想死好想死
Has been a near-death experience.

61
00:02:33,101 --> 00:02:35,492
做开胃菜 然后...
Make the appetizers. And then we'll be...

62
00:02:35,962 --> 00:02:40,080
如果真出了啥意外 我希望他一下解决了我
If an accident does happen, I hope he kills me...

63
00:02:41,123 --> 00:02:44,822
因为我觉得我不会是个乐观向上的残障人士
Because I don't think I would be a very inspiring disabled person.

64
00:02:46,017 --> 00:02:47,622
亲爱滴 放亲松
Honey, relax.

65
00:02:47,652 --> 00:02:48,919
她还没来
She's not here yet.

66
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:50,626
你最好蛋定一下 别猴急猴急的
You might want to play it a little cooler.

67
00:02:50,657 --> 00:02:52,414
要不会把你女朋友吓跑的
You don't want to scare off your girlfriend.

68
00:02:52,445 --> 00:02:53,927
她才不是我女朋友
She's not my girlfriend!

69
00:02:53,947 --> 00:02:57,340
她只是过来跟我一起研究蚕的生命周期
She's just coming over to study the life cycle of silkworms.

70
00:02:58,586 --> 00:02:59,915
嗷 她到了
Oh. She's here.

71
00:02:59,945 --> 00:03:02,040
她到了 那啥 我头发不乱吧
She's here! okay, how's my hair?

72
00:03:02,081 --> 00:03:03,358
是谁说只是朋友来着
I thought it was just a friend.

73
00:03:03,358 --> 00:03:04,350
我可听到了
I heard that.

74
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,831
我故意的
I wasn't whispering.

75
00:03:05,862 --> 00:03:08,253
曼尼去开门 让她感受什么叫宾至如归
Manny, open the door. Make her feel welcome.

76
00:03:08,284 --> 00:03:10,092
凯莉 早上好
Kelly! Good morning.

77
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:11,247
欢迎你来我家
Uh, I'm glad you're here.

78
00:03:11,247 --> 00:03:12,647
这是我妈
Um, this is my Mom.

79
00:03:12,678 --> 00:03:13,771
很高兴认识你哦
Nice to meet you!

80
00:03:13,771 --> 00:03:14,895
在我们的文化里
In my culture,

81
00:03:14,895 --> 00:03:17,051
母亲都灰常粘儿子
mothers are very clingy to their sons.

82
00:03:17,082 --> 00:03:20,229
其实呢 哥伦比亚妇女死亡的首要原因
In fact, the leading cause of death among Colombian women

83
00:03:20,291 --> 00:03:22,498
就是她们的儿子要结婚
is when their sons get married.

84
00:03:22,539 --> 00:03:24,787
但是我不会这样
But I'm not like that.

85
00:03:24,807 --> 00:03:26,933
我只要曼尼高兴就好哩
I just want my Manny to be happy.

86
00:03:26,974 --> 00:03:30,632
曼尼 叫你的朋友凯莉吃肉卷馅饼
Manny, why don't you give your friend Kelly an empanada?

87
00:03:30,683 --> 00:03:31,909
不了 谢谢
Oh, no, thank you.

88
00:03:31,909 --> 00:03:34,781
我尽量避免摄入反式脂肪
I try to stay away from trans fats.

89
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:36,600
哎呀呀 就吃一个没啥滴啦
Oh, I'm sure one won't make a difference.

90
00:03:36,651 --> 00:03:38,183
这是曼尼的最爱哟
They're Manny's favorite!

91
00:03:38,224 --> 00:03:41,596
我 我也不要吃反式脂肪了
I... think I'm going to stop eating trans fats, too.

92
00:03:46,246 --> 00:03:48,371
妈 这是在哪拍的
Mom? When was this from?

93
00:03:48,964 --> 00:03:51,805
这是我跟你爸去看玫瑰杯的时候拍的
Oh... That's the year your dad and I went to the rose bowl.

94
00:03:51,805 --> 00:03:53,654
-那场老精彩了 -是啊
- Incredible game. - Yeah.

95
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:55,862
妈 你看起来真美
Mom, you look really pretty.

96
00:03:55,913 --> 00:03:57,282
谢谢你 宝贝儿
Thank you, sweetheart.

97
00:03:57,313 --> 00:03:58,907
那后来怎么回事
So, what happened?

98
00:03:58,907 --> 00:04:01,073
小卢克 人人都会变老嘛
Well, Lukey, everyone gets older.

99
00:04:01,339 --> 00:04:03,045
即便你妈的风采不再
Just 'cause parts of your mom aren't what they used to be,

100
00:04:03,045 --> 00:04:04,016
也不代表...
it doesn't meam...

101
00:04:04,016 --> 00:04:06,039
我是想问比赛后来怎么样了
I mean, what happened in the game?

102
00:04:08,379 --> 00:04:10,270
我们输给了宾州队
We got our butts kicked by Penn state.

103
00:04:10,301 --> 00:04:11,854
但是游行非常棒
The parade was awesome, though.

104
00:04:11,895 --> 00:04:13,898
是安吉拉·兰斯伯里担任司仪
Angela Lansbury was the grand marshal.

105
00:04:13,989 --> 00:04:16,411
"美好的记忆" 她写道
"Good time," she wrote.

106
00:04:16,442 --> 00:04:18,108
行了 继续收拾
Okay, come on, guys. Let's get back to it.

107
00:04:18,148 --> 00:04:19,957
堆着这么多东西没人会买的
No one's gonna buy this heap looking this way.

108
00:04:19,988 --> 00:04:22,175
恶 妈妈 垃圾丢哪边
Hey, mom, which one is the garbage can?

109
00:04:22,205 --> 00:04:23,769
丢...
Um, it...

110
00:04:24,116 --> 00:04:25,751
乖乖 这个不能丢
Honey, you can't throw that away.

111
00:04:25,751 --> 00:04:26,558
这是小毯毯
It's blankety.

112
00:04:26,558 --> 00:04:28,030
可它有够恶心
It's disgusting.

113
00:04:28,030 --> 00:04:30,268
怎么会 亲爱的 你以前可喜欢它了
No, sweetie, you loved blankety.

114
00:04:30,298 --> 00:04:31,954
你上哪儿都要带着它
You wouldn't go anywhere without him.

115
00:04:31,974 --> 00:04:33,425
哈 直到卢克吐在上面
Yeah, until Luke threw up on it.

116
00:04:33,456 --> 00:04:34,713
哈哈
Yeah.

117
00:04:34,723 --> 00:04:36,573
我年轻的时候老吐
I used to throw up all the time.

118
00:04:36,614 --> 00:04:38,402
还记得呕吐桶桶吗
Remember buckety?

119
00:04:39,454 --> 00:04:40,834
看这个
Oh, look at this.

120
00:04:40,875 --> 00:04:42,080
这是什么
What is that?

121
00:04:43,102 --> 00:04:44,635
那天咱们去海边
We went to the beach one day,

122
00:04:44,676 --> 00:04:46,331
卢克玩得很开心
and Luke had such a good time.

123
00:04:46,383 --> 00:04:48,835
所以他要带一罐阳光回家
That he wanted to being home a jar of sunshine.

124
00:04:48,855 --> 00:04:50,674
这样他就能永远记着了
So he could always remember it.

125
00:04:50,695 --> 00:04:52,003
还记得吗 亲爱的
Do you remember, honey?

126
00:04:52,003 --> 00:04:53,934
不 不不 别 别打开
Oh, no... no, no, don't... don't open it.

127
00:04:53,965 --> 00:04:55,661
你真以为你把阳光收进罐子里了
You really think you trapped sunshine in there?

128
00:04:56,397 --> 00:04:57,807
我现在通知你们
I'm just letting you know now,

129
00:04:57,807 --> 00:04:59,657
你们死了之后我绝对不会管他的
I'm not taking care of him when you guys die.

130
00:04:59,697 --> 00:05:01,618
别说了 这样做很可爱的
Stop. It's sweet.

131
00:05:01,649 --> 00:05:02,978
还热热的好吧
Still feels hot.

132
00:05:04,173 --> 00:05:05,982
刚看车那家伙来电话了
Hey! It's that guy who came by earlier.

133
00:05:06,023 --> 00:05:07,229
貌似很想买
He was really interested.

134
00:05:07,229 --> 00:05:08,557
他叫啥来着 快告诉我
What was his name? Shoot!

135
00:05:08,598 --> 00:05:11,060
做销售千万不能忘记客户姓名
Well, you can't be in sales and not remember people's names.

136
00:05:11,101 --> 00:05:14,361
所以我用"迷你联想"来帮助记忆
That's why I like to use what they call "minimonic" devices.

137
00:05:14,361 --> 00:05:16,497
这是帮助记忆的小诀窍
They're little tricks to help you remember.

138
00:05:16,497 --> 00:05:19,297
就像那天 我认识了个家伙叫卡尔
Um, like the other day, I met this guy named Carl.

139
00:05:19,297 --> 00:05:21,065
现在我或许忘了他的名字
Now, I might forget that name,

140
00:05:21,065 --> 00:05:23,078
但我记得她穿着一件Grateful Dead的汗衫
But he was wearing a Grateful Dead T-shirt.

141
00:05:23,078 --> 00:05:24,447
有什么乐队像Grateful Dead
What's a band like the Grateful Dead?

142
00:05:24,447 --> 00:05:25,877
Phish 鱼生活在哪里
Phish. Where do fish live?

143
00:05:25,877 --> 00:05:26,644
海洋
The ocean.

144
00:05:26,644 --> 00:05:28,422
什么东西生长在海洋
What else lives in the ocean?

145
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,474
珊瑚
Coral.

146
00:05:29,474 --> 00:05:31,416
你好 卡罗
Hello, "Coral".

147
00:05:33,644 --> 00:05:35,585
我记得这是"助记口诀"
I think it's "mnemonic".

148
00:05:36,536 --> 00:05:38,886
啊… 我觉得我没记错
I... I think I'd remember.

149
00:05:38,916 --> 00:05:40,623
行吧
Okay.

150
00:05:40,664 --> 00:05:42,043
老爸 你一定行的
You can do it, dad.

151
00:05:42,074 --> 00:05:43,300
好吧
Okay.

152
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,721
他看起来像是个外国鼓手
He looked like the drummer from foreigner.

153
00:05:44,751 --> 00:05:45,651
这个外国人来自法国
Now, foreigner's from France.

154
00:05:45,651 --> 00:05:46,877
法国和蚂蚁押韵[英文单词读音]
France rhymes with "ants."

155
00:05:46,877 --> 00:05:48,144
蚂蚁破坏了野餐
Ants ruin a picnic.

156
00:05:49,023 --> 00:05:50,494
哈啰 Nick[和野餐后缀音同]
What's up, Nick?

157
00:05:51,966 --> 00:05:53,652
是吗
Really?

158
00:05:53,682 --> 00:05:54,949
真的吗
Really?

159
00:05:54,949 --> 00:05:56,278
那太好了
Well, that's great.

160
00:05:56,298 --> 00:05:58,301
随时欢迎 我们一整天都在
Yeah, no, swing by anytime. We're here all day.

161
00:05:58,342 --> 00:05:59,497
谢谢
Thanks.

162
00:06:00,018 --> 00:06:00,978
你猜怎么着
Guess what?

163
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,869
谁说哥卖不出去
You said I couldn't sell this?

164
00:06:02,910 --> 00:06:04,729
你自打嘴巴了吧
Well, you're gonna be eating a humble pie.

165
00:06:04,749 --> 00:06:07,457
高兴不起来了吧 真对不住了嘿
Stuffed with crow and a big side of sorry,

166
00:06:07,457 --> 00:06:08,213
我给它卖了
'cause I just did.

167
00:06:08,213 --> 00:06:12,229
当你的面卖出去了 叫你老否定咱爷们
In your face, girl with the negative tattoo!

168
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:16,235
亲爱的
Honey...

169
00:06:16,235 --> 00:06:17,063
等等
Wait.

170
00:06:17,063 --> 00:06:17,911
不
No!

171
00:06:17,911 --> 00:06:21,119
有人输不起了
Whoa. Someone doesn't like to lose.

172
00:06:24,461 --> 00:06:25,871
宝贝
Honey.

173
00:06:25,922 --> 00:06:27,251
宝贝儿
Honey!

174
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:28,221
对不起
I'm sorry.

175
00:06:28,232 --> 00:06:29,591
对不起
I'm sorry.

176
00:06:29,621 --> 00:06:31,859
今早一睁眼 我还很烦那辆车
When I woke up this morning, I hated that car,

177
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,463
就连想起它都让我抓狂
and even thinking about it made me mad.

178
00:06:33,494 --> 00:06:35,507
但是我们一起经历了这么多
But then when we were going through it,

179
00:06:35,538 --> 00:06:37,377
还有那个可爱的小毯毯…
and blankety...

180
00:06:37,377 --> 00:06:39,053
所有这一切 我只是
all that stuff... I just...

181
00:06:39,073 --> 00:06:42,395
一想到那些美丽的日子就这样随车而逝了
The thought of that whole part of our life driving away...

182
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,898
我们可以留着小毯毯嘛
We can keep blankety.

183
00:06:44,898 --> 00:06:45,859
但我不想...
I don't want...

184
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:47,729
看看他们
Look at them.

185
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,387
好像昨天他们还都只是小宝宝
Come on. A minute ago, they were babies.

186
00:06:51,387 --> 00:06:52,961
今天呢 连车都会开了
And now they're driving.

187
00:06:53,298 --> 00:06:54,974
然后我们也不久于人世了
And soon we'll all be dead.

188
00:06:54,974 --> 00:06:58,009
打住 你咋能忽略掉死前的美好时光呢
Whoa! You're leaving out a few great minutes there.

189
00:06:58,029 --> 00:06:59,868
退休啊 颐养天年啊
Retirement, old age...

190
00:06:59,899 --> 00:07:02,280
超级酷的爬楼梯自动椅子啊
Cool chair that goes up the stairs.

191
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,354
是啊 对不起
Yeah. I'm sorry.

192
00:07:04,354 --> 00:07:06,500
我不该胡思乱想
I'm... being ridiculous.

193
00:07:06,531 --> 00:07:09,535
不用道歉 我就喜欢你充满着人情味
Don't apologize. I love you when you're human.

194
00:07:09,566 --> 00:07:11,037
听着
Listen.

195
00:07:11,068 --> 00:07:13,112
听我说
Hey! listen!

196
00:07:14,788 --> 00:07:16,647
车不卖了
We don't have to sell the car.

197
00:07:16,678 --> 00:07:18,671
亲爱的 当然要卖
Oh, sweetie, of course we do.

198
00:07:18,671 --> 00:07:19,938
没理由要留着它
It doesn't make any sense to keep it.

199
00:07:19,968 --> 00:07:22,452
那我该怎么做才能让你感觉好点
Well, what can I do to make you feel better?

200
00:07:22,452 --> 00:07:23,586
什么也不用做
Nothing.

201
00:07:23,811 --> 00:07:25,486
除非你给我造一台时光机
Unless you can build me a time machine.

202
00:07:27,193 --> 00:07:29,053
亲爱的
Honey...

203
00:07:29,431 --> 00:07:31,454
除非有人能想办法
Until someone can figure out how to keep a wormhole

204
00:07:31,495 --> 00:07:32,956
阻止虫洞的倒塌
from collapsing in on itself.

205
00:07:32,997 --> 00:07:34,152
否则就是痴人说梦
That's just a pipe dream.

206
00:07:35,225 --> 00:07:37,013
是啊
Sure.

207
00:07:37,054 --> 00:07:38,720
菲尔 想都别想 菲尔
Phil! come on back, phil.

208
00:07:42,827 --> 00:07:44,687
我找到了...
Well, I found the...

209
00:07:44,687 --> 00:07:46,240
我找到了射钉枪
I found the nail gun.

210
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,651
噢 太好了
Oh. Yay.

211
00:07:47,692 --> 00:07:49,797
奇怪的是 它给裹在一条旧毛巾里
The weirdest thing... it was wrapped in an old towel

212
00:07:49,817 --> 00:07:52,116
塞在盒子里 在壁橱最顶上
stuffed in a box on the top shelf of the closet.

213
00:07:52,137 --> 00:07:54,068
赶紧把它放在柜台上
Well, just set it down on the counter.

214
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:55,376
小心
Heads up!

215
00:07:55,376 --> 00:07:57,011
老爸 你来这干嘛
Oh, dad, what are you doing here?

216
00:07:57,052 --> 00:08:01,293
我只是来还歌洛莉亚借的电锅
I'm, uh, just, uh, returning that crockpot that Gloria borrowed.

217
00:08:01,323 --> 00:08:03,571
我都忘了这码事了 杰
Oh, yeah, I forgot you had that crockpot, Jay.

218
00:08:03,571 --> 00:08:06,095
我们正准备给莉莉建造一座公主城堡
Well, we're just getting ready to build Lily a princess castle

219
00:08:06,095 --> 00:08:06,719
如果你...
if you...

220
00:08:06,719 --> 00:08:07,884
-想帮忙 -当然 没问题
- Want to help? - Yeah, sure.

221
00:08:07,884 --> 00:08:09,835
只要你不介意的话 米奇尔
Oh. Well, if it's okay with you, Mitchell.

222
00:08:09,866 --> 00:08:11,378
好啊 我没问题 老爸
Oh, yeah! oh, no, dad.

223
00:08:11,378 --> 00:08:12,717
还记得当初我们一起做书架的时候吗
Oh, remember how much fun we had

224
00:08:12,748 --> 00:08:14,199
多美好的回忆呀
when we built that bookshelf together?

225
00:08:15,854 --> 00:08:17,969
那简直就像打了场越战
That was my vietnam.

226
00:08:18,511 --> 00:08:20,657
我确实参加过越战
And I was in vietnam.

227
00:08:21,249 --> 00:08:23,692
看看我们哦
Oh! Look at us!

228
00:08:23,733 --> 00:08:26,114
我们就是工匠三兄弟
Three construction dudes!

229
00:08:26,144 --> 00:08:27,851
老爸 我去给你拿几副专用手套
Dad, I'm gonna get you some workman gloves.

230
00:08:27,871 --> 00:08:30,477
我有蓝色的和驼色的
I have a blue and camel.

231
00:08:30,477 --> 00:08:31,131
你喜欢哪个颜色的
What's your preference?

232
00:08:31,162 --> 00:08:32,357
你懂的
Surprise me.

233
00:08:32,357 --> 00:08:33,542
如果我们把东西都整理到同一个笔记本上
Wouldn't it be easier

234
00:08:33,542 --> 00:08:35,300
那不就轻松多了
if we had all our stuff in the same notebook?

235
00:08:35,351 --> 00:08:36,720
你这么觉得
You think?

236
00:08:36,751 --> 00:08:39,071
这样我们就省的总是来回翻了
I mean, we're always going back and forth.

237
00:08:39,101 --> 00:08:41,309
我把我的笔记夹到你的本子上
I'll just put my things in your notebook.

238
00:08:41,309 --> 00:08:41,728
好的
okay.

239
00:08:41,728 --> 00:08:44,027
谁想喝巧克力奶呀
Who wants chocolate milk?

240
00:08:44,068 --> 00:08:45,222
我要 妈妈
Sure, mom.

241
00:08:45,222 --> 00:08:47,184
-进度如何呀 -好极了
- So how is it going? - Great!

242
00:08:47,215 --> 00:08:48,216
凯莉在把她的笔记
Kelly's moving her stuff

243
00:08:48,216 --> 00:08:49,024
都搬到我的本子上
into my notebook.

244
00:08:49,616 --> 00:08:50,710
速度还真快啊
This is sudden.

245
00:08:51,476 --> 00:08:52,866
应该的
It just felt right.

246
00:08:53,193 --> 00:08:54,378
你应该这样
Oh, you know what you should do?

247
00:08:54,419 --> 00:08:56,320
在巧克力奶里放一撮盐
Put a pinch of salt in the chocolate milk.

248
00:08:56,361 --> 00:08:57,853
提味得多
It really brings out the flavor.

249
00:08:57,893 --> 00:08:59,191
吃爆米花才用盐呢
Salt is for the popcorn.

250
00:08:59,191 --> 00:09:00,520
听起来对味
That sounds good.

251
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,052
你不会喜欢的
You wouldn't like it.

252
00:09:02,686 --> 00:09:05,016
也许我们该让曼尼自己决定
Maybe we should let Manny decide.

253
00:09:05,864 --> 00:09:07,080
好滴
Okay.

254
00:09:07,877 --> 00:09:09,011
给你盐
Here's the salt.

255
00:09:09,042 --> 00:09:10,902
我们看他选哪个
We'll see what he likes.

256
00:09:28,038 --> 00:09:29,735
天啊
Wow!

257
00:09:29,776 --> 00:09:31,012
好喝翻了
That's really good!

258
00:09:31,012 --> 00:09:32,913
妈妈 你试试
Try it, mom!

259
00:09:39,759 --> 00:09:41,844
老娘对这无爱
I don't care for it.

260
00:09:43,172 --> 00:09:45,318
其实很好喝
It was delicious.

261
00:09:45,349 --> 00:09:46,851
终于把莉莉哄睡了
I finally got Lily down for a nap.

262
00:09:46,892 --> 00:09:47,515
米奇尔在哪里
Where is Mitchell?

263
00:09:47,515 --> 00:09:49,181
怎么能没人看着他呢
He's not supposed to be unsupervised!

264
00:09:49,181 --> 00:09:49,743
没事
Don't worry.

265
00:09:49,743 --> 00:09:52,073
我让他去车库给塔顶插旗子
I got him in the garage putting flags on the spires.

266
00:09:52,103 --> 00:09:53,217
哦 那就好
Okay, perfect.

267
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:54,883
这样最好 省的有人受伤了
It's better that way. Nobody gets hurt.

268
00:09:54,934 --> 00:09:56,671
插旗子这事儿也省了
We don't have to put flags on the spires.

269
00:09:56,671 --> 00:09:57,529
是啊
Yeah.

270
00:09:57,529 --> 00:09:59,042
好了 我们来盖上屋顶
All right, let's get this roof on.

271
00:09:59,083 --> 00:10:00,462
应该咔嚓就扣上了
It's supposed to snap right into place.

272
00:10:01,852 --> 00:10:03,528
嘿
Hey!

273
00:10:03,558 --> 00:10:05,009
你干的怎么样了 电锯哥[电锯惊魂里的杀人狂]
Whatcha got going on over there, Jigsaw?

274
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,655
我觉得我得从吊桥开工
Well, I thought that I would get started

275
00:10:06,655 --> 00:10:08,944
屋顶就归你们了 所以...
on the, uh, drawbridge while you guys worked on the roof, so...

276
00:10:08,984 --> 00:10:10,313
你的旗子都插好了吗
You all done with the flags?!

277
00:10:10,313 --> 00:10:11,468
当然
Yeah!

278
00:10:11,468 --> 00:10:13,143
十五分钟就搞定了
Yeah, it took me like 15 minutes.

279
00:10:13,174 --> 00:10:15,013
哪里像你说的那么麻烦
It was a lot easier than you made it out to be.

280
00:10:15,054 --> 00:10:16,260
杰 怎么办
Do something, Jay.

281
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:18,048
米奇
Uh, Mitch?!

282
00:10:18,089 --> 00:10:20,031
干嘛
Yeah.

283
00:10:22,258 --> 00:10:23,709
你去弄点三明治吧
How about you make us some sandwiches?

284
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:25,293
不成 不成 我们还没完工呢
No. No, we're in the middle of this.

285
00:10:25,334 --> 00:10:26,295
不是 杰的意思是说
No, I think what Jay's saying is,

286
00:10:26,295 --> 00:10:27,255
你为什么不挑点螺栓来
why don't you go sort some bolts?

287
00:10:27,276 --> 00:10:28,604
不用 我已经挑好了
No, I sorted the bolts.

288
00:10:28,635 --> 00:10:29,963
-全部吗 -一共就六个
- All of 'em? - There were six.

289
00:10:30,025 --> 00:10:31,455
你们俩不对劲啊
W... what's going on with you two?

290
00:10:31,486 --> 00:10:32,937
难道 是想把我甩开不成
Are you... are you trying to get rid of me?

291
00:10:32,968 --> 00:10:34,899
呃 米奇
Uh..., Mitch.

292
00:10:34,930 --> 00:10:36,636
天 你们真是闲我碍事
Oh, my god. You are.

293
00:10:36,667 --> 00:10:38,884
你们 居然狼狈为奸
You're... you're, like, in cahoots.

294
00:10:38,915 --> 00:10:42,358
米奇尔 你一碰工具 我就害怕
Mitchell, I get scared, when you're around tools,

295
00:10:42,358 --> 00:10:44,136
亲爱的 这太危险了
Honey, it's dangerous...

296
00:10:44,167 --> 00:10:46,078
对你 对我
For me, for you,

297
00:10:46,078 --> 00:10:47,999
对我们的花花 都是威胁
for... our roses.

298
00:10:48,510 --> 00:10:49,675
孩子 他说得对
Works better this way, kid.

299
00:10:49,675 --> 00:10:51,933
我是指 顺利建好城堡
I mean, castle goes right up,

300
00:10:51,933 --> 00:10:53,292
没人给一切两半
Nobody gets sliced in half.

301
00:10:53,323 --> 00:10:55,459
你们也太小看人了吧 我可是…
Do you know how insulting this is? I was...

302
00:10:56,307 --> 00:10:58,759
我可是在歌鸟夏季剧院实习过的
I was an intern at the songbird summer playhouse.

303
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,803
你们以为南海仙境那出戏
Do you think that the town of Brigadoon

304
00:11:00,844 --> 00:11:02,070
就嗖一下变出来了吗
just magically appeared?

305
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:04,267
当然戏里看着是这么回事 但是 那个布景
Well, in the play, it did, but...the set...

306
00:11:04,308 --> 00:11:07,200
那个布景是我用这双手搭的
the set was built with these two hands!

307
00:11:08,314 --> 00:11:09,499
米奇尔 米奇尔
Mitchell. Mitchell...

308
00:11:09,499 --> 00:11:12,575
还有范特普庄园 艾维塔的阳台
The Von Trapp mansion, Evita's balcony...

309
00:11:12,606 --> 00:11:14,159
算了 算了
Okay. Okay.

310
00:11:14,189 --> 00:11:15,354
你这是要去哪
Oh, where are you going?

311
00:11:15,354 --> 00:11:16,530
我要暴走了
I'm going on a walk,

312
00:11:16,530 --> 00:11:18,543
哈 没错 我还能自己走
and, oh, yeah, I can still do that by myself.

313
00:11:18,573 --> 00:11:21,578
看着嘿 哦 好害怕会摔倒哦
Watch. Oh, I hope I don't get hurt.

314
00:11:21,608 --> 00:11:24,163
哦 妈呀 谁这么缺德放个门柱在这儿
Oh, god, who put that doorjamb there?

315
00:11:24,193 --> 00:11:25,277
害我没看见
I didn't see it.

316
00:11:25,277 --> 00:11:26,973
直接撞上去了
I ran right into it.

317
00:11:29,487 --> 00:11:32,859
哎呀 糟糕 绊着了 走路好难的说
Oh, no, I tripped! Walking is so hard!

318
00:11:32,890 --> 00:11:34,443
刚才那下可不像是故意的
That one didn't look like it was on purpose.

319
00:11:34,484 --> 00:11:35,894
就是故意的
It was!

320
00:11:37,192 --> 00:11:39,419
还有几步路
Just a few more steps.

321
00:11:39,419 --> 00:11:40,410
对不起!
Oh, sorry!

322
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:41,432
有台阶 有台阶 对不起
Step! Step! Sorry!

323
00:11:41,432 --> 00:11:42,556
-菲尔 -对不起 对不起
- Phil?! - Sorry, sorry.

324
00:11:42,556 --> 00:11:43,578
这一跤绝对值
It's gonna be worth it.

325
00:11:43,578 --> 00:11:44,580
绝对不值
No, it's not.

326
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:45,622
别听她瞎说
Don't listen to her.

327
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:46,593
开...
And...

328
00:11:46,593 --> 00:11:49,648
-嗷 嗷 嗷 -对不起 不要乱动
- Ow. Ow. Ow! - Sorry. Don't struggle.

329
00:11:50,261 --> 00:11:51,416
不要乱动
Stop struggling.

330
00:11:53,521 --> 00:11:54,952
好惊喜啊 我们的车
Great. It's our car.

331
00:11:54,982 --> 00:11:56,311
不只是车哦 孩子们
Not a car. Kids?

332
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:59,141
"时" 什么
"ti... " what?

333
00:11:59,182 --> 00:12:02,176
今天晚上 克莱尔·邓菲 我们把时钟拨回
Tonight, Claire Dunphy, we are turning back the clock

334
00:12:02,217 --> 00:12:03,494
那纯真年代...
to a simpler time...

335
00:12:03,494 --> 00:12:06,131
当年那个咱一家挤在旅行车里
when families piled into their station wagons,

336
00:12:06,172 --> 00:12:07,500
捎上一些汉堡
picked up some burgers,

337
00:12:07,510 --> 00:12:10,392
去郊外野餐的日子
and went on a picnic up to granger point.

338
00:12:10,433 --> 00:12:12,323
亲爱的 没必要吧
Honey, we don't have to do this.

339
00:12:12,374 --> 00:12:13,427
她说得对
Listen to her.

340
00:12:13,427 --> 00:12:15,522
不啊 会很好玩的 我跟那个
No, it's gonna be great. I talked to...

341
00:12:15,583 --> 00:12:16,911
法国 蚂蚁 野餐%￥%@&*...
France, ants, picnic...

342
00:12:16,942 --> 00:12:19,803
尼克说了 他明天才来取车
Nick, and he's not picking up the car till tomorrow.

343
00:12:19,824 --> 00:12:21,949
我们还能来一次家庭大聚会
We have one more night of family fun!

344
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:23,502
能有啥意思
What's gonna be fun about it?

345
00:12:23,502 --> 00:12:24,187
谁说不是
Listen to him

346
00:12:24,187 --> 00:12:25,567
-啥都有意思 -啥也没意思
- Only everything. - Only nothing.

347
00:12:25,567 --> 00:12:27,355
好了 小朋友们
Okay, kids, you know what?

348
00:12:27,355 --> 00:12:28,632
你们老爹要做好人好事
Your father is trying to do something nice,

349
00:12:28,642 --> 00:12:30,890
你们少抱怨点儿多好
so I would appreciate it if you would stop your whining

350
00:12:30,921 --> 00:12:33,006
赶紧上车
and just get in the car.

351
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:35,663
屡试不爽
Still does it!

352
00:12:35,693 --> 00:12:36,766
啊哈
Oh, my!

353
00:12:36,766 --> 00:12:38,084
快点 快点进去
Come on, get in, get in!

354
00:12:41,845 --> 00:12:44,032
我不得不说 他得学会释怀
I'm just saying, the kid's gotta learn to let things go.

355
00:12:44,062 --> 00:12:46,178
这对米奇尔是个敏感话题
Well, this is a touchy subject for Mitchell.

356
00:12:46,218 --> 00:12:48,865
他就想体现男子汉的一面 就像咱俩
He wants to feel like a regular joe, like you and I.

357
00:12:48,865 --> 00:12:49,805
哦 不好意思
Oh, pardonnez-moi.

358
00:12:49,815 --> 00:12:52,125
比起普通香槟 我更倾向于第戎香槟
I prefer the champagne Dijon to the standard yellow.

359
00:12:53,566 --> 00:12:56,069
要证明自己是纯爷们 方法很多 你懂的
You know, there are a few areas that define us as men,

360
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,992
比如运动健身 还有木工啥的
like sports and construction.

361
00:12:58,992 --> 00:13:00,749
米奇尔只是想证明自个是
Mitchell just wants to feel like he's...

362
00:13:00,749 --> 00:13:01,740
爷们俱乐部中的一员
part of the man club.

363
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:03,692
你俩不就那地儿认识的
Isn't that where you guys met?

364
00:13:03,723 --> 00:13:05,889
我知道你这开玩笑是因为基佬氛围让你不适
I know you're making a joke because you're uncomfortable,

365
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,064
我当没听见
so I'll let it slide.

366
